1 DAILY CRAWL - web direct reading (zero key, read-only, one fetch)
  source: https://developers.weixin.qq.com/miniprogram/dev/api/payment/wx.requestVirtualPayment.html
  read  : official API page, fetched 2026-11-02 06:2x +08:00, no login, no key
  got   : the parameter table and the full error-code table, which the tree had
          never read (until today only the FAMILY NAME was recorded):
          signData Object required, passed as a STRING of JSON, e.g.
            '{"offerId":"123","buyQuantity":1,"env":0,"currencyType":"CNY",
              "productId":"testproductId","goodsPrice":10,
              "outTradeNo":"xxxxxx","attach":"testdata"}'
          offerId string required | buyQuantity number required
          env number optional 0 live / 1 sandbox, default 0
          currencyType string required, only CNY legal
          productId string, required only when mode=short_series_goods
          goodsPrice number (fen), required only when mode=short_series_goods,
            used to check the price against the console item price
          activitySellingPrice number optional (fen), must travel with goodsPrice
          outTradeNo string required, 8-32 chars, [A-Za-z0-9 _-|@], not leading _,
            one use only, and the page itself says uniqueness is not guaranteed
            in extreme cases so business must not depend on it
          attach string required, passed through to the delivery notification
  code  : 1001 / -1 / -2 / -4 / -5 / -15001 / -15002 / -15003 / -15004 / -15005 /
          -15006 / -15007 / -15008 / -15009 / -15010 / -15011 / -15012 / -15013 /
          -15014 / -15016 / -15017 / -15018 / -15019 / -15020 / -15021
  three constraints the design must honor, read off the page:
    (a) -15011 says the LIVE build accepts env=0 only, sandbox env=1 is refused,
        so a sandbox leg cannot be assumed to exist in production;
    (b) -15002 + the outTradeNo note: one use only AND not a uniqueness law,
        so the idempotency key stays ours, not the order number;
    (c) -15013: goodsPrice is checked against the console item price, so the
        19.9 price must exist as a published item before any order is sent.
  consumer: P-47 item 4 pay-integration design (docs/spec/) field-level gate;
          BLUEPRINT section 4 payment route note; bootstrap physical checklist
          gains "publish item + price in console before first order".

